| Pricing discipline | When the order book looked thin last winter, did your pricing hold or did you sharpen your pencil to keep the lads busy? | Priced tight to fill the diary, now carrying contracts that are costing more to run than they'll ever pay back | A pricing floor that holds regardless of order book pressure, with a pipeline that doesn't depend on buying work |
